==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kh₂eyd-}}

Borrowing from {{bor|en|NL.|incīsor}}, from {{af|la|incīdō|-tor|t1=to cut into, cut through|t2=-er, -or|pos2=agent noun suffix|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈsaɪ.zə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incisor.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪzə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy|zootomy}} A [[narrow]]-edged [[tooth]] at the front of the [[mouth]] of [[mammal]]s, between the [[canine]]s and [[adapt]]ed for [[cut]]ting; in [[human]]s there are four in each [[jaw]].

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|incise}}
* {{l|en|incision}}
{{rootsee|en|kh₂eyd}}

